                        "glosses": [
                            "зоол. представитель одноимённой группы паразитических первичнополостных беспозвоночных животных"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b239e90-0edc-474a-b625-a62ae1b44402",
                                "sense_id": "a0507966-22e9-3896-8cb4-933e04e7e081",
                                "text": "◆ Немательминты у морских рыб представлены двумя классами — нематодами и скребнями. А.В. Гаевская, А.А. Ковалева, «Болезни промысловых рыб Атлантического океана», 1975 г."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bce0c787-22df-4ee3-87c7-c2ee4383de93",
                        "source_entry_id": "09112995-72a9-31f3-8f48-8c90a4dedd6a",
                        "source_sense_id": "a0507966-22e9-3896-8cb4-933e04e7e081",
                        "target_lang_word": "acanthocephalan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "acanthocephalan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93a23fba-5993-3fdb-97e5-6cc172d1e5a9",
                                        "entry_id": "fbc53334-324e-31b7-9525-e734ba53f344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of parasitic intestinal worms comprising the phylum Acanthocephala."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d81834e-a1db-40f8-952e-0d8d3582eb52",
                                                "sense_id": "93a23fba-5993-3fdb-97e5-6cc172d1e5a9",
                                                "text": "That discussion of fish intestines is justified because many acanthocephalans have been described from fish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7d2fa2f-edf4-457e-9e7a-24ac8dd52561",
                                                "sense_id": "93a23fba-5993-3fdb-97e5-6cc172d1e5a9",
                                                "text": "2006, B. B. Nickol, Phylum Acanthocephala, P. T. K. Woo (editor), Fish Diseases and Disorders, Volume 1: Protozoan and Metazoan Infections, 2nd Edition, page 458,\nClearly acanthocephalans contain large amounts of lipid and possess enzyme systems for lipid metabolism (Filipponi et al., 1994; Weber et al., 1995); however, use of these lipid deposits in energy metabolism is yet to be demonstrated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "775660d9-5a74-4109-b7c2-11c8b29ab8ff",
                                                "sense_id": "93a23fba-5993-3fdb-97e5-6cc172d1e5a9",
                                                "text": "Acanthocephalans are dioecious pseudocoelomate worms remarkably adapted to a parasitic lifestyle in that there is no mouth or digestive system."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "acanthocephalan",
